WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:05.230
"Echo" isn't just a cool name for a superhero;
it also reflects how the character and the

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:08.490
series embrace the past to forge a new future.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.100
Here's how the ending of "Echo" brings it
all together.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.360
"Echo" takes place directly after the events
of "Hawkeye."

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.970
In that show, Maya Lopez learns from Clint
Barton that Kingpin anonymously hired him,

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:23.859
as Ronin, to assassinate her father and several
other members of the Tracksuit Mafia.

00:00:23.859 --> 00:00:28.510
Maya then leaves Kingpin's organization and
confronts her former friend Kazi Kazimierczak,

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:32.559
killing him during the Tracksuit Mafia's battle
against Clint and Kate Bishop.

00:00:32.559 --> 00:00:36.890
Maya later ambushes Fisk and shoots him, seemingly
putting an end to New York City's greatest

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.230
gangster.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:42.320
When "Echo" picks up, Maya returns to her
hometown of Tamaha, Oklahoma to take over

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.309
Fisk's operations there.

00:00:44.309 --> 00:00:48.320
She locks horns with her Uncle Henry, who,
like Maya's father, was involved with Kingpin's

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.770
organization against his will.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:54.980
After attracting unwanted attention from the
Kingpin's henchmen, Maya discovers that Fisk

00:00:54.980 --> 00:01:00.079
is alive, and he offers her a chance to return
to New York and resume operations as his "Queenpin."

00:01:00.079 --> 00:01:05.070
"You want an empire, you'll have it."

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:09.120
All the while, Maya is also having recurring
visions of her ancestors, including the first

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:14.010
Choctaw woman, Chafa, as well as Tuklo, a
Choctaw warrior from the 1800s.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:18.100
She's also confronting her strained relationships
with her family members, including her cousin

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:22.659
Bonnie, whom she avoided contact with following
her father's death, and her grandmother Chula,

00:01:22.659 --> 00:01:26.090
whose anger towards Maya's father left them
estranged.

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:30.350
Maya learns the truth about her visions from
Chula, realizing that her ancestors are contacting

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.470
her during critical moments.

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:36.820
She later confronts Kingpin in his hotel room
and nearly accepts his offer to kill him,

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:40.740
calling back to his own experience of killing
his father to free himself from an abusive

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:42.009
household.

00:01:42.009 --> 00:01:43.620
Maya refuses.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:48.080
Most of the finale centers on Tamaha's Choctaw
Nation Powwow, a festival celebrating their

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:49.360
ancestry.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.640
The Tracksuit Mafia arrive in search of Maya,
forcing Henry and Maya's cousin Biscuits to

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.290
hold them off.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:59.180
Wearing a costume given to her by Chula, Maya
gets cornered by Kingpin and his henchmen,

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:02.079
who have taken Chula and Bonnie hostage.

00:02:02.079 --> 00:02:06.460
Kingpin threatens to kill them so that he's
the only family Maya has left, but Maya uses

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:11.090
her ancestral powers for the first time to
not only fight off Fisk's goons, but to empower

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:13.710
Chula and Bonnie to fight alongside her.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:18.310
Finally, Maya takes control of Fisk's mind,
sending him back to pivotal moments in his

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:21.900
life, including the moment before he decided
to kill his father.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.290
She encourages him to let go of his pain.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:29.510
Fisk, terrified of Maya's powers and perhaps
his own memories, abandons his plan and escapes

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:31.540
with his remaining henchmen.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:35.930
Before Maya leaves Tamaha, she visits her
family at a barbecue and is warmly welcomed,

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:38.580
all of them now free from Kingpin's control.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:43.560
"Echo" involves Maya completing her transformation
from villain to superhero.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:47.420
Characters such as Wanda Maximoff and Loki
have made the transition from villain to hero,

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:51.879
and occasionally back, putting Maya in good
company among the Marvel Cinematic Universe's

00:02:51.879 --> 00:02:55.239
roster of evildoers turned good guys.

00:02:55.239 --> 00:02:56.790
"Again.

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.340
Faster."

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:02.540
When Maya is introduced in "Hawkeye," she's
relentlessly chasing down Ronin for killing

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.690
her father, targeting Kate Bishop and later
Clint Barton.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:10.100
Audiences can still empathize with Maya during
this villain arc, though, especially after

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:14.780
flashback sequences show her father encouraging
her to adapt to a world that won't accept

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:15.780
her.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:20.230
When Fisk turns up alive in "Echo," Maya must
choose between her family and her ambition.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:25.150
It raises the question: Why does Maya choose
to be a hero rather than the "Queenpin"?

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:29.360
The answers lie in the flashback sequences
depicting Maya's history working for Kingpin,

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:32.430
where she misinterprets his affection for
her as paternal.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.260
It's actually strategic.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:38.330
Fisk is no stranger to using cruel, manipulative
tactics against those close to him.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:42.470
Case in point, in episode 4 of "Echo," he
brings Maya her favorite cookies to entice

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:44.200
her into listening to him.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:48.709
The only difference is, this time around,
Maya is too wise to trust Fisk.

00:03:48.709 --> 00:03:52.150
After all, she didn't pour out an expensive
bottle of wine for no reason.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:53.989
"It came highly recommended."

00:03:53.989 --> 00:03:59.640
"Hawkeye" only briefly examines Maya's history
with Wilson Fisk, revealing that her father,

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:03.480
William, was Fisk's partner in operating the
Tracksuit Mafia.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.540
Fisk took on the role of an uncle figure in
Maya's life.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:10.120
This is fleshed out much further through flashback
sequences in "Echo."

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:14.590
In one important flashback in episode 4, Fisk
is surprised when a young Maya joins him in

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:17.160
assaulting a rude ice cream vendor.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:21.470
This is the start of Maya's transformation
into one of Fisk's closest commanders.

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:25.250
This establishes that Kingpin saw something
in Maya early on that made her a valuable

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:27.400
asset to his criminal empire.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.250
He never had to lure her into his world of
corruption.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.230
She was a willing participant.

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:36.310
Even the act of Fisk assaulting the vendor
proves that his love for Maya is genuine,

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:39.840
though still as toxic as any of Fisk's other
relationships.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:45.230
No more is this apparent as in Fisk's relationship
to American Sign Language, or ASL, the only

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:47.250
way for him and Maya to communicate.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:51.960
While every other character in "Echo" is fluent
in ASL, Fisk is not, which Maya calls him

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.380
out on as evidence that he doesn't truly care
about her.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:59.820
Comic Basics interpreted this as an example
of Fisk's shortcomings as a character, writing,

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:04.320
"Kingpin was likely incapable of truly bonding
with people, and since Maya saw him as some

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:08.150
kind of heroic personality when she was little,
Kingpin liked it."

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:12.750
Family is a major theme in "Echo," with one
of the very first scenes depicting the traumatic

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:15.590
car crash that tore Maya's family apart.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:19.870
When Maya returns to Tamaha, tensions run
high between her and her relatives.

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:24.509
There's her Uncle Henry, who is still involved
in Fisk's organization; her grandmother, Chula,

00:05:24.509 --> 00:05:29.590
who turned her back on Maya and her father
years ago; and Bonnie, Maya's closest childhood

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:32.980
friend who she's desperate to keep away from
the criminal world.

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:36.120
Along the way, Maya is plagued with visions
of her ancestors.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:39.130
She eventually embraces them and is rewarded
with superpowers.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:44.430
"Echo" shows that Maya is stronger, both literally
and figuratively, when she accepts her family,

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:46.280
her past, and her flaws.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:50.280
She tries to pass this on to Kingpin during
their final fight, forcing him to relive his

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.060
most painful memories.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:56.680
When Maya encourages Fisk to let go of his
pain, Fisk instead runs away, appearing more

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:59.560
like a frightened child than an intimidating
crime lord.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:01.870
"What did you do?"

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:04.980
The strength of families has been a part of
the Marvel Cinematic Universe throughout its

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:08.830
many phases, from the very first "Thor" movie
to 2021's "Eternals."

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:13.389
While tragedy and trauma might make many people
run away from the ones they love the most,

00:06:13.389 --> 00:06:18.060
"Echo" shows that Maya is her best self when
she's fighting to protect them.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:22.480
Fans eager to see Maya Lopez come into her
own as a superhero in "Echo" had to wait a

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:23.480
bit.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:26.710
It takes all five episodes for the character
to embrace her heroic side.

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:30.970
It's not until her conversation with Chula
in episode 4 that Maya learns that her powers

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:33.009
come from her ancestors calling to her.

00:06:33.009 --> 00:06:54.090
"Generations are echoing, reaching out to
us at a time when we need them the most."

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:58.220
Some critics felt the explanations for Maya's
superhero abilities were underdeveloped, with

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.520
The Ringer writing,

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:03.210
"Lopez's superpowers [...] manifest late in
the season but are never really explained

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:05.430
or demonstrated clearly."

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:09.370
There are many different powers showcased
among the Lopez women, from her mother's ability

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:14.330
to heal, to Maya's ability to force others
to experience visions, as she does with Kingpin.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:19.000
Ultimately, it appears that Maya's superpowers
are gifts given to her by her ancestors.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:23.379
While the exact details of what she can do
remain unclear, the important distinction

00:07:23.379 --> 00:07:27.639
is that Maya is being aided along her journey
by the strong Choctaw women who came before

00:07:27.639 --> 00:07:28.639
her.

00:07:28.639 --> 00:07:31.830
The main lesson from Maya's story is that
she is stronger when she embraces that she's

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:35.970
living as a result of her family's past, not
in spite of it.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:40.750
In the series, Maya's superpowers are rooted
in Choctaw mythology, with her oldest ancestor

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:44.250
Chafa becoming a heroic figure of the Choctaw
creation myth.

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:48.750
Many aspects of Choctaw mythology play an
integral role in shaping Maya's powers.

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:53.069
This comes as a huge shift for those familiar
with the character from Marvel Comics.

00:07:53.069 --> 00:07:57.650
Maya first appeared in 1999, sent by Kingpin
to antagonize Daredevil.

00:07:57.650 --> 00:08:01.070
The two adversaries eventually became romantically
entangled.

00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:04.600
Maya's connections to Kingpin in the comics
are similar to those in the series.

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:07.700
However, one massive change comes with her
powers.

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:12.720
In the comics, Maya has photographic reflexes,
allowing her to copy her opponents' movements.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:17.050
This is, coincidentally, a similar ability
to Taskmaster, who appeared as an antagonist

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.199
in 2021's "Black Widow."

00:08:19.199 --> 00:08:22.630
It's not the first time Marvel has done this
with their characters, as they made similar

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:26.600
changes to Kamala Khan in the 2022 series
"Ms. Marvel."

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:31.350
Her abilities were also reinterpreted to fit
her cultural background and ancestral history.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:35.260
"Echo" director and executive producer Sydney
Freeland explained the change as an attempt

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:38.240
to be more representative of Choctaw history.

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.070
Freeland told Variety in 2023,

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:43.449
"Her power in the comic books [is] kind of
lame.

00:08:43.449 --> 00:08:47.390
[...] Representation was extremely important
to myself and to everyone on the crew."

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:52.279
"Echo" is one of Marvel's more ambitious projects,
despite also being its shortest at only five

00:08:52.279 --> 00:08:53.279
episodes.

00:08:53.279 --> 00:08:57.780
As the show's star Alaqua Cox told Collider,
the emotional scenes with Vincent D'Onofrio

00:08:57.780 --> 00:08:59.320
towards the end were challenging.

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:00.460
As she put it,

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:04.050
"I remember looking on the call sheet for
the next day and seeing how it was such an

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:06.670
intense, emotional scene, and I said, 'Oh,
crap.'"

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:10.310
Naturally, though, she also hoped the show
left fans wanting more, stating,

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:14.420
"We never know where Maya is gonna go next,
so I think that they'll all be curious about

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:15.420
that."

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:19.310
The supporting actors in "Echo" also felt
somewhat intimidated by the project.

00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:23.149
Also speaking to Collider, Devery Jacobs,
who plays Bonnie, singled out the finale's

00:09:23.149 --> 00:09:25.190
Pow-Wow as a daunting set piece, saying,

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:29.540
"It was done so beautifully by our director,
Sydney Freeland, who is just, like, a rock

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:32.650
star in all of it, and I don't think that
we could have brought it home with anyone

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:33.650
else."

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:37.870
Vincent D'Onofrio also described to Entertainment
Weekly how the final scene of Kingpin sets

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:40.399
up a promising future for his character when
he said,

00:09:40.399 --> 00:09:43.839
"There are so many places to go with this
character, it's crazy."

00:09:43.839 --> 00:09:47.730
D'Onofrio also feels optimistic about his
return in "Daredevil: Born Again."

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:48.730
He continued,

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:52.500
"The reception of 'Echo' so far is helping
everybody understand that this is a really

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:54.090
good tone for 'Daredevil' too.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:58.709
I think 'Born Again' is heading in that direction
in a major way now."

00:09:58.709 --> 00:10:02.510
There are plenty of other firsts with "Echo,"
and one of them has to do with branding.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:07.110
The show is designated as a "Marvel Spotlight,"
which is meant to signify that a certain show

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:11.430
or movie can be watched as a standalone project,
even if you're not familiar with the rest

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:13.090
of the MCU.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:16.530
Because "Echo" is the first to be labeled
as such, its success will likely determine

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:20.649
Marvel's ambition in moving forward with future
"Marvel Spotlight" projects.

00:10:20.649 --> 00:10:24.750
The show's success, unfortunately, may also
determine Maya Lopez's future in the Marvel

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:26.860
Cinematic Universe at large.

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:30.800
Unlike other Marvel series, "Echo" does not
end with confirmation that Maya Lopez will

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:34.680
return — and considering the character's
current irrelevance to the larger Multiverse

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:39.269
Saga of Phases 4 through 6, she might just
remain a supporting cast member in future

00:10:39.269 --> 00:10:40.540
projects.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:44.370
One of those may be "Daredevil: Born Again,"
in which Charlie Cox and Vincent D'Onofrio

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.220
will both be appearing.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:50.089
There's certainly a lot of stories to be told
involving Maya Lopez, if her comic book history

00:10:50.089 --> 00:10:51.120
is any indication.

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:55.440
At one point, the character dons the mantle
of Ronin, and at another time, she becomes

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:57.680
a host for the Phoenix Force.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:01.110
Maya was also nearly included in the "Moon
Knight" series as a potential love interest

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:05.529
for Oscar Isaac's Marc Spector, so it's possible
that those two characters could cross paths

00:11:05.529 --> 00:11:06.760
at some point.

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:10.620
Of course, it wouldn't be a Marvel Cinematic
Universe installment without a hint as to

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:11.930
what's coming up.

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:15.930
In a mid-credits scene for the final episode
of "Echo," Vincent D'Onofrio's Kingpin sits

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:19.360
on his private jet waiting to take off and
return to New York.

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:23.180
His attention is caught by a news program
on the plane TV, in which New York City's

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:25.260
mayoral election is being discussed.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:31.050
"A bare-knuckle brawler would do well in this
race, an outsider, someone who is not afraid

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:32.430
to take on the establishment."

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:36.490
The look on Fisk's face seems to indicate
that he intends to join the campaign — and

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:40.130
knowing how powerful he is in New York City,
he'll likely win.

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:43.399
This could set the stage for Fisk's role in
"Daredevil: Born Again."

00:11:43.399 --> 00:11:47.350
Despite reports of creative overhauls in recent
months, D'Onofrio confirmed on Twitter the

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:49.670
changes are all positive, telling Variety,

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:53.010
"Frankly I'd be worried if we were settling
for less."

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:56.660
This would make "Daredevil: Born Again" an
adaptation of an integral Kingpin storyline

00:11:56.660 --> 00:12:00.839
from Marvel Comics, in which Wilson Fisk becomes
the mayor of New York City and furthers his

00:12:00.839 --> 00:12:04.050
plans to resurrect his dead wife, Vanessa.

00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:08.180
Fisk's new position could also find him at
odds with other NYC-based superheroes, such

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:11.760
as Spider-Man, Doctor Strange, and Kate Bishop
— yet again.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:15.870
"Echo" is certainly one of the more exciting
projects in the Marvel Cinematic Universe's

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:17.170
recent output.

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:21.269
Whether it's because of the focus on a deaf,
disabled, Indigenous character or its depiction

00:12:21.269 --> 00:12:25.779
of violence more akin to the beloved Netflix
shows, it certainly feels like a step forward.

00:12:25.779 --> 00:12:30.350
The biggest step, though, is the involvement
of the Choctaw nation during the show's development.

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:32.630
As director Sydney Freeland described to Deadline,

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:36.560
"The Choctaws were so crucial ... because
they had their own written histories or oral

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:40.730
histories and cultures and traditions that
were drawn from, and it really was a collaboration

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:44.019
between myself, our production and the Choctaws."

00:12:44.019 --> 00:12:46.180
That didn't go unappreciated by Marvel.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:50.140
Right before the credits roll on "Echo," a
title card specifically thanks the Choctaw

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:53.100
Nation of Oklahoma for their consultations
on the project.

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:56.600
The collaboration didn't stop at the development
stage, either.

00:12:56.600 --> 00:13:00.600
Marvel has included a Choctaw language dub
of "Echo" on streaming services, and members

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:04.910
of the Choctaw Nation went into detail regarding
their work with Marvel on the Nation's official

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:05.920
website.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:09.970
It's quite possible that we could see more
Native American Marvel characters appear on-screen

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:11.900
soon, like Wyatt Wingfoot or Warpath.

